  />Minneapolis, 1984. A new era of music television is creating overnight
  stars. A magnetic young performer known as &ldquo;The Kid&rdquo; seems
  like the perfect frontman to lead his bandmates to stardom. But when his
  past threatens everything he&rsquo;s built, he&rsquo;ll have to sing his
  way out of the darkness and into the spotlight where he belongs.<br /><br
  />A visionary creative team reimagines Prince&rsquo;s extraordinary world
  for the stage, with direction by Tony&reg;-nominated director Saheem Ali
  (<em>Buena Vista Social Club</em>), acclaimed librettist and screenwriter
  Peter Duchan (Dogfight), Emmy&reg;-winning choreographer Ebony Williams
  (<em>Sneakerella</em>, additional choreography for the Renaissance World
  Tour), a music team led by Tony Award winner Jason Michael Webb (<em>MJ
  the Musical</em>), and longtime Prince collaborators and bandmates Bobby Z
  and Morris Hayes?as Prince music advisors.</p>
END:VEVENT
